### 11\. Cybersecurity investigation filters

| Filter                                   | Function                                   |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0 | Initial TCP SYN packets                    |
| tcp.flags.reset == 1                     | TCP resets                                 |
| tcp.analysis.retransmission              | Retransmission investigation               |
| tcp.analysis.zero_window                 | TCP zero-window conditions                 |
| dns.flags.rcode != 0                     | DNS errors                                 |
| icmp.type == 3                           | Destination unreachable messages           |
| ip.ttl <= 2                              | Very low IPv4 TTL                          |
| tcp.len > 1000                           | TCP segments carrying more than 1000 bytes |
| frame.len > 1500                         | Frames larger than 1500 bytes              |
| tcp.stream eq 0                          | Packets in TCP stream number 0             |

These filters help investigate connectivity problems, unusual traffic and network behaviour. They do not independently prove an attack.

